{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>and all the men who were Korah's</b> – He had acquired for himself male slaves and maidservants, and members of his household who were Egyptians, Cushites, and Canaanites, purchased with his money, and they were punished as part of their property, for they were stricken in their persons and in their wealth. And perhaps there were also Israelites in his house, gerim and toshavim, who were drawn after his counsel and were punished, for Scripture does not allude to his offspring, since it is written: \"and the sons of Korah did not die\" (Numbers 26:11), for they were grown, righteous and good men, and their merit stood for them, and he did not have small sons and daughters, for Scripture did not mention any little children in connection with Korah."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:21.765387992Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}